# jemdoc: menu{MENU}{research.html}
= Ajay U. Mandlekar -- Research
[https://ee.stanford.edu Department of Electrical Engineering], [https://stanford.edu Stanford University]

== Recent News

- \[December 2020\] We recently extended [https://roboturk.stanford.edu/ RoboTurk] to enable [https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.06733 human-in-the-loop teleoperation] and developed Intervention Weighted Regression, a simple and effective algorithm to learn from such interventions. We showcase results on two challenging contact-rich manipulation tasks requiring precision to solve.

- \[December 2020\] We recently extended [https://roboturk.stanford.edu/ RoboTurk] to enable [https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.06738 multi-user collaborative teleoperation] on challenging multi-arm tasks. We collected datasets on novel two-arm and three-arm tasks and developed a residual policy framework to address the problem of learning from multi-user demonstration data.

- \[December 2020\] Check out our new preprint on [https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.08424 Deep Affordance Foresight], a new model that extends the classical definition of affordance to enable long-horizon planning.

- \[September 2020\] We released [https://robosuite.ai robosuite] v1.0, a modular simulation framework and benchmark for robot learning.

- \[July 2020\] We are organizing the [https://sites.google.com/utexas.edu/rss-2020-imitation-learning/home?authuser=0 Advances and Challenges in Imitation Learning for Robotics] workshop at [https://roboticsconference.org/ RSS 2020].

